    },
    {
      "id": "claim_642cbb4c6742474082833fb9e21826ec",
      "statement": "The success-path view is an approximation reconstructed by build_views from the event store alone (not from the engine's DAG): it finds the derive event(s) that produced target_id, prefers rules other than TARGET-REACHED, builds a by_out index of derive events keyed by fact_id, walks backwards from the last producer through each event's inputs pushing every producer of each input, dedups by event object id, and reverses the result to derivation order.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://trace.py#L26-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8e1d4c554abdba440e25c7ec3d64aa4d90e5180937bd3a7b31c84bdf3793f3f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1b9f75b17b524b81a60ba78b96e675ce",
      "statement": "When the target has no derive producer at all (it is a given, or the run ended unknown), build_views does not fabricate a chain: the success path contains only terminal unknown or deadend events whose fact_id equals target_id, or whose fact_kind equals _find_target_kind(trace) — the fact_kind of the first deadend in the store.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://trace.py#L37-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81211e9260edd8d7336743abcf5e5ad328771ffe367a5d2c18abb4e8425e9bf1:"
        },
        {
