    {
      "id": "claim_bef45ebf1222450ba4ee77810b9f3f62",
      "statement": "The solver's returned note is discarded at the engine boundary in v1 — both modes unpack out_fact, _note = rule.apply(inputs) and never write the note into the trace; a solver failure returning (None, note) without raising produces a None-valued derived fact that can never satisfy the known-fact scan, so the outcome stays 'not a wrong number', and the note reaches the trace only as an exception path's reject reason.",
      "evidence": [
