    {
      "id": "claim_e2bf2425dc1c4af1b8c3663a7c86f811",
      "statement": "Trace-storage scaling is an [open] question: the full-verbosity store is unbounded on large search spaces, with when/how to rotate, summarize, or time-box verbose ingestion while preserving audit integrity deliberately unresolved; the current stance assumes problem-scale usage, no rotation or summarization is implemented in trace.py/engine.py/CLI, and any resolution would change trace.py and ARCHITECTURE.md §4.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ARCHITECTURE.md#L358-L361",
